rmdir() of Cosmopolitan on Windows (libc/calls/unlinkat-nt.c, C68 of
docs/UPSTREAM.md): when RemoveDirectory() fails because the directory
is not empty, the libc waits 1, 2, 4 ... 1024 ms and tries again, about
2 s in all. The wait is for a file whose deletion still waits, for
example a file that another program has open. For a directory with a
real file, the wait does not help, and rmdir() took about 2 s to fail.
Now, before each wait, the libc opens each entry of the directory. When
one entry opens, the directory has a real entry, and rmdir() fails at
once with ENOTEMPTY. An entry whose deletion waits does not open, and
then the libc waits as before.

The file has no #ifdef __x86_64__, so scripts/steps.sh builds one object
for both halves with this patch (build_cosmo_file).

